 <!--
   INTENTIONAL: the package name (pcov_enhanced) differs from the extension it
   provides (<providesextension>pcov</providesextension> below). This is by
   design: we publish under a distinct product identity while shipping the
   drop-in `pcov` extension, so `pecl package-validate` emits a
   "providesextension name differs from package name" warning. That warning is
   EXPECTED and correct — do NOT rename the package or the providesextension to
   silence it, or the build would stop being a drop-in pcov replacement.
 -->
 <name>pcov_enhanced</name>
 <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
 <summary>An alternative pcov build adding branch and path coverage (like Xdebug, far faster).</summary>
 <description>
pcov_enhanced is a drop-in alternative to the pcov extension. It builds and
loads as the "pcov" extension, so line coverage behaves exactly like upstream
pcov, and existing tooling keeps working unchanged.

Setting pcov.mode=branch additionally collects branch and path coverage in the
same shape php-code-coverage consumes, so `phpunit --path-coverage` works while
keeping pcov's very low overhead — orders of magnitude faster than Xdebug path
coverage.

This is an unofficial, community distribution based on krakjoe/pcov.
 </description>
