 <!--
   RELEASE DATE: PECL requires a literal date in the manifest and warns if it is
   not "today" at package time. Bump this to the current UTC date (YYYY-MM-DD,
   `date -u +%F`) on every release / when regenerating the tarball, or have the
   release workflow set it. Stale dates only trigger a validator warning, not an
   error, but keep it current to publish cleanly.
 -->
 <date>2026-09-12</date>
 <version>
  <release>1.1.0</release>
  <api>1.1.0</api>
 </version>
 <stability>
  <release>beta</release>
  <api>stable</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="http://www.php.net/license">PHP-3.01</license>
 <notes>
Adds opt-in branch and path coverage via pcov.mode=branch:
 - Branch/path analysis ported from Xdebug 3.6, matching its output shape.
 - Optional xdebug-compatible surface so unmodified phpunit --path-coverage
   selects this extension (dormant unless pcov.mode=branch; never overrides a
   real Xdebug; reports phpversion('xdebug') as the sentinel 3.99.0-pcov).
 - Line coverage and the default behaviour are unchanged from upstream pcov.
 </notes>
